Verify the systemwide shared library directories are group-owned by "root" with the following command:

$ sudo find /lib /lib64 /usr/lib /usr/lib64 ! -group root -type d -exec stat -c "%n %G" '{}' \;

If any systemwide shared library directory is returned and is not group-owned by a required system account, and is not documented with the information system security officer (ISSO) as an operational requirement, this is a finding.
